{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice","id":1205331,"title":"So how does using money as a focus for Matter/Prime work in practice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-10T12:39:16-07:00","id":1205331,"title":"So how does using money as a focus for Matter/Prime work in practice?","content":"I'm looking at the Sons of Ether book, and one of the pregen characters uses money for Matter and Prime effects. How does that work in practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:24:50-07:00","id":1205352,"title":"","content":"Buy stuff. You can make stuff out of nothing. Who are you buying from? The universe itself! Turns out they accept American Express too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:32:17-07:00","id":1205355,"title":"","content":"Ain't that the ex Syndicate woman?<br /> <br /> I imagine she uses money much like Syndicate uses it. Honestly, I too find hard to imagine this focus in practice but I think the trick it's to treat money as a token you exchange and try to pass some sort of supernatural mojo as a result of the transaction. Imagine money as a sort of &quot;net&quot; that you use to capture &quot;value&quot; (magick) which you can use to crreate effects<br /> <br /> I.E: Fuel your mojo with the value that money represents (Prime), expend a lot for that coat to get sure it's of exeptional quality (Matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-10-2018, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:50:26-07:00","id":1205372,"title":"","content":"Soooo....if you were in a game, what in detail would you describe your character doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:08:06-07:00","id":1205380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205372#post1205372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo....if you were in a game, what in detail would you describe your character doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>As an Etherite, my explanation would be that the universe is fundamentally a system to trades and balances, and so it's possible to obtain anything in exchange for something of equal or greater value.<br /> <br /> I'd probably put the money in at a box, type into a keypad the kind of object I want, and as long as it equalled the money in the box, it would turn into the item I want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:32:32-07:00","id":1205388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205380#post1205380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an Etherite, my explanation would be that the universe is fundamentally a system to trades and balances, and so it's possible to obtain anything in exchange for something of equal or greater value.<br /> <br /> I'd probably put the money in at a box, type into a keypad the kind of object I want, and as long as it equalled the money in the box, it would turn into the item I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the Etherite thing... SCIENCE! Equivalent Exchange is... well I mean I accept &quot;this thing spins, therefore science&quot;, since it's thematic and cool. A series of tubes and glowy things which spin making lightning is awesome, and technobabble explains that.<br /> <br /> Putting... money in a... in a box. And then just stating what you... want? Beyond being horribly Vulgar no matter how you try and sell it, it's also just a bit out of place no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:34:35-07:00","id":1205389,"title":"","content":"Money would be a great Focus for Mind. People are greedy, and accept bribes. Well Magick can exploit this quite easily. Money can be a great tool for many Mind effects which involve affecting others. To make it more useful, expand from just &quot;money&quot; to &quot;valuable objects&quot;. Now your Mind 4 &quot;marry me&quot; rote will go off without a hitch, thanks to this Diamond Ring...<br /> <br /> As for Prime, Primal Utility has money as an important feature. Money can come highly charged with Quintessence if you perform business correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:35:47-07:00","id":1205391,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a Virtual Adept who uses a vast array of crypto-currencies and transfers them to identityless shell accounts as a way of performing magic. Different accounts have different effects - he's not sure who or what owns the accounts, just that if he transfers money to the account along with a brief request something will happen. For example in our last session we were stuck at a high security door. My character pulled out his smart phone, took a picture of the door and then transferred currency to one of the accounts along with the picture and the request, &quot;Please open!&quot; and the door suddenly popped open. <br /> <br /> Mechanically this is was just a Matter/Forces/Entropy rote which can cause certain high tech devices to suddenly activate after he transfers X number of some kind of crypto-currency to a specific account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T18:59:27-07:00","id":1205435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice#post1205331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking at the Sons of Ether book, and one of the pregen characters uses money for Matter and Prime effects. How does that work in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime is, among other things, a highly valuable and rare energy source, so even if you can't use dollar bills to soak up quint directly, you can use money to buy the equipment that lets you manufacture tass or enchant an item.<br /> <br /> * &quot;I can build that laser gun (read: Artifact) for you, but the exotic reactor you'd need to keep the thing operating would cost a small fortune&quot; (Prime)<br /> <br /> * &quot;I've got a nanotech process that will construct food or metals from raw etheric energies. Just need to buy some exotic materials to power the initial fabricators.&quot; (Matter/Prime)<br /> <br /> * &quot;Transparent aluminum? Sure, sure, no problem, no problem at all. Ah, er, the chemicals I need <i>do </i>run a bit pricey, and I left my wallet in my other ethersuit...&quot; (Matter)<br /> <br /> As with Syndicate ops, your character doesn't necessarily need the technical knowhow; they can have a bevy of contacts and business partners who can do the impossible, all of them merely held back by a lack of funding. Note that M20 generally expects these &quot;focus characters&quot; to be substantiated as a Background; Revised doesn't seem to.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate can also use Matter/Prime to simulate being in a hypertech supply chain - i.e. you &quot;create&quot; the item (the effect) but the actual in-universe action is using $$$ to pay a high-tech manufacturer to print you whatever you want and a cutting-edge delivery service to drone drop it at your feet within the hour. There's no real reason other technomancers couldn't do roughly the same. If you need it <i>now </i>you can go vulgar and use exotic methods to have it teleported to you (or, as the example in the Syndicate book suggests, use cutting-edge VirtAdept math to refine it out of raw nothingness with sophisticated models.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T19:27:01-07:00","id":1205439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205388#post1205388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't the Etherite thing... SCIENCE! Equivalent Exchange is... well I mean I accept &quot;this thing spins, therefore science&quot;, since it's thematic and cool. A series of tubes and glowy things which spin making lightning is awesome, and technobabble explains that.<br /> <br /> Putting... money in a... in a box. And then just stating what you... want? Beyond being horribly Vulgar no matter how you try and sell it, it's also just a bit out of place no?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Science! to work, all you need is a theory. Not all Etherites are gears, electrodes, and steam engines. If your theory is that the value of money and the value of an object makes them inherently linked in some way. In the same way that one can turn lead into gold just be rearranging the molecular makeup of the lead to resemble gold, so too then can you rearrange the physical make up of substances to reflect their inherent monetary value. If that's the case, then it should be possible to go the other way, and turn them back from monetary value into real objects.<br /> <br /> Currently all objects exist in a state of &quot;value&quot; that lies beyond our physical plane. In order to bring these items forth, we require a way of transferring their &quot;value&quot; state into a &quot;physical&quot; state, and the best way to do that is to convert them via the following equation.<br /> <br /> Object = Money^(e x SquareRoot(Time)) where e is the exponential constant.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, it is a well known that Time is in some way equatable to money, and though some...lesser scientists may disagree, it is quite possible to convert the lengths and measures of time into a value containing the same units as money. In this way, we can simplify this equation and work out the exact monetary value of the object as it exists within this &quot;value&quot; state. Once that is worked out, we can then begin the process of converting the &quot;Value&quot; state of the object into the &quot;physical&quot; state we are more familiar with. This can be described by the application of a very familiar formula used for the Theory of Relativity, here adapted for our purposes.<br /> <br /> VObj = PObj(C^2)<br /> <br /> Where VObj is the number given for our &quot;value&quot; state, PObj is the number for our &quot;physical&quot; state, and C is the universal constant known better to some as the Speed of Light, which, as I'm sure everyone is well aware, mediated by the transfer of particles within the ether that exists all around us. This formula describes the Value state to be the same as the Physical state which has been exposed to the universal constant, i.e. the Physical state transfers to the Value state becoming exposed to the particles of light within the ether to an extreme degree. This may be the reason why objects which are burnt begin to lose value. As they burn, their Physical state is transformed into the Value state, and what is left then contains less monetary worth than what it was before being burned. The fire allowed a greater amount of ether to interact with the object, and thus, for lack of a better term, it &quot;bled&quot; value. Physical state worth transformed into Value state worth, joining the epherial realm and thus leaving behind only that which had less exposure to the Ether.<br /> <br /> So how would one reverse this process and turn a pure Value state back into a Physical state? Well, as with any equation, you would need to perform a little algebra.<br /> <br /> PObj = VObj / (C^2)<br /> <br /> So while Value states are objects which have received a great deal of ether, Object states must then be Value which have been removed from Ether.<br /> <br /> Now that presents a problem because Ether is in essence all around us. In order to get an object into being, we would have to in some way remove Ether exposure. However, there is another problem. In order for the object to come into being, we would need something to have that objects same amount of value. Now, in theory you could use any objects of equal value for this, however in practice the value of individual objects is so specifically small and ever fluctuating, that it is simply more practical to use cash, especially as cash can be devided into several denominations such as the farthing, and the ha-penny, making it far more ideal for this kind of intricacy.<br /> <br /> To make this work then, we would need:<br /> <br /> A) Some way to equate the Value state of the object we are trying to transform towards the Physical state<br /> B) A way in which to remove Ether from the system so as to allow the conditions for such a transformation to take place.<br /> <br /> And this, ladies and gentlemen, is precisely what I have done. By placing the exact worth of the Value state of the object you wish to transform within this tightly sealed Ether Isolation Cage enthused Box, We can create the exact conditions necessary to conjure practically any object we would need. In many ways, it's like paying the universe for an instant delivery.<br /> <br /> The values converge, and once the box is open the object is solid enough to remain Physical even after being reintroduced to Ether.<br /> There may be a few paradox bugs around, especially if the object itself receives too much ether in too short a time, but then this principle still needs a little more exploration before it can be fully understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T21:46:45-07:00","id":1205461,"title":"","content":"Remember that a mage with sufficient money can just BUY hypertech, provided they have a supply chain in place or sufficient teams of unAwakened but Hypertech educated researchers/tech people. Just like other mages might have what M20 calls Minimum Abilities to do many of their Effects, a mage employing Hypereconomics (like a Syndicate op or a former Syndicate Etherite) might make use of Minimum Background scores to do theirs. Retainers, Spies, Cult (of personality), Influence, Requisitions, Contacts, and, yes, Resources. All of these can allow an Enlightened person to do great things.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Syndicate, they believe that &quot;you get what you pay for&quot;. Given that the Syndicate bankrolls the rest of the Union, it's not surprising Syndicate ops believe entirely in the efficacy of the technology the other Conventions produce. The tech better work, they paid enough for it. So while a more coincidental application of Matter + Prime would be to use supply chains to have materials produced and transported over, a more vulgar application might involve just turning on the hypertech devices (if not Devices) and letting the tech earn its price tag. Teleporters, atomic reconstructors, 3D printers, and good ol' nanomachines (son) will make something from nothing in a flash. It's going to invite Paradox, because the Syndicate op is &quot;buying prototypes ahead of when their bugs are worked out&quot;, but it can be helpful in a pinch.<br /> <br /> If you're an Etherite employing these methods, it's largely the same principle. Sure, the supply chain isn't as regulated and expansive in the Society of Ether as it is in the whole of the Technocratic Union. But the Etherites DO have supply chains - even the most brilliant Progressive Scientist won't be building an Ether Ship in his basement, at least not without help. Whole heck of a lot of Consors, Acolytes (or &quot;lab assistants&quot;), and techno-Sorcerers running around, helping more Enlightened Etherite scientists do their work.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Etherites tend to generate more ideas and plans than they have time or resources to implement. There's likely a brisk trade in blueprints among Etherites, just as the Order of Hermes has its brisk trade in Hermetic treatises. Designs for gadgets that only require a bit of manpower to put together. A sufficiently wealthy Etherite who doesn't have enough time to invent himself could always buy these blueprints, hire Consor lab techs to construct them, and then pick up the results afterwards. Sure, there's little prestige in using the inventions of others, but some Etherites (like the Adventurers) see the actions they perform with powerful tech to be more important than making it. (You think Batman sits in his cave and invents all his own stuff? Not likely, when there are CRIMES that need fighting! That's the advantage of being rich.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T22:39:03-07:00","id":1205467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205461#post1205461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. (You think Batman sits in his cave and invents all his own stuff? Not likely, when there are CRIMES that need fighting! That's the advantage of being rich.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of? I mean I imagine he designs most of it. Alot of magickal Batman's awakened effects involve a large factory producing his toys though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T23:11:54-07:00","id":1205473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205467#post1205467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of? I mean I imagine he designs most of it. Alot of magickal Batman's awakened effects involve a large factory producing his toys though</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Batman is certainly smart enough to design his own stuff. The problem is that time spent in the lab is time he can't spend out in the field, punching the Riddler in the face. Until he takes his crime-fighting crusade into the stage where he's not personally going out to do it, he takes a hands-on approach. Which means he has to offload as much of the logistical work as he can. That means funding research and development (with many of the findings being funneled where possible into legitimate scientific research), and having his tools produced separately (either by contractors who are kept in the dark as to what they are ultimately building, or a series of automated assembly lines).<br /> <br /> At a certain point, Batman turned himself into a minor NGS (Non-Governmental Superpower), complete with aircraft/landcraft production, weapons development, biotech research, cyber surveillance, and even a space program (for shuttling to Justice League space bases, and putting stuff like Brother Eye into orbit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:36:37-07:00","id":1205502,"title":"","content":"I think the example of a Syndicate member using money for Mind procedures is excellent, and it makes perfect sense to use it as a focus for that.<br /> <br /> What I myself am actually struggling with is the idea of using Money for aformentioned Matter/Prime effects under the Syndicate paradigm.<br /> As was explained before, the Syndicate member essentially uses money as a focus for an investment that, using some already existing supply chain or another, produces the item he wants. Okay, alright.<br /> <br /> But.<br /> <br /> My simple question is: &quot;How does this make the action any different from any unawakened big investor?&quot;<br /> 1) Toss enough money into existing supply chain<br /> 2) Get result.<br /> Or, put differently, it would not matter if the money comes from the Syndicate member or some unwakened money spender, the already established (possibly Hypertech educated) supply chain would be able to create the same items from the investment.<br /> So where does the Syndicate's member's actual Matter/Prime sphere expertise come in? If it's about an awakened sense of investment, it sounds to me more like a Mind 1 effect to boost your Wits/Intelligence and then making an excellent choice.<br /> <br /> All actual requirements for Matter/Prime spheres would be more technical in my mind - establishing the supply chain itself, for example.<br /> <br /> EDIT.<br /> You could of course say that the money as a focus gets used by the Syndicate member to produce a Matter/Prime effect that subtly influences the workings of the supply line to produce amazing results - probably even unbeknownst to the Syndicate member themself when it comes to the details - but this would then simply come from the Syndicate member's basic paradigm of 'Invest value to get good value'. It is hard to imagine how the Syndicate suit actually gains their detailed knowledge in the spheres. Of course you could say that the spheres on the sheet get increased values from the suit's growing experience in investments..<br /> <br /> Parts of the Syndicate paradigm remain, ironically, the most exotic and esoteric part of Mage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-11-2018, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T02:40:29-07:00","id":1205514,"title":"","content":"Maybe when Syndicates buy something from even a mundane shop, the item turns out to be simply flat-out better than what others buy, because it\u2019s the Syndicate who does the buying? They know the worth of their money, so their every use of it is worth it. Alternatively, the buying Syndicate \u2018knows\u2019 that his secret hand signals, marked cash and encoded credit cards prompt the seller to turn aside the mundane items and present the top-grade ones. The seller, on the other hand, knows nothing except that somehow he felt he had to do that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m no expert in Ascension, so dunno if that even makes sense. This was mainly inspired by the extra material for Mage Translation Guide that didn\u2019t make it into the book (written by Dave Brookshaw, IIRC), where it presents an alternate version of Acanthus (mages specializing in Time and <i>Fate</i>) as the Syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:16:21-07:00","id":1205519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205514#post1205514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe when Syndicates buy something from even a mundane shop, the item turns out to be simply flat-out better than what others buy, because it\u2019s the Syndicate who does the buying? They know the worth of their money, so their every use of it is worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a Syndicate member doing that - that's not a problem.<br /> My problem is that, if a relatively rudimentary (if enlightened) belief of the power of Value is enough to make this work...then every Syndicate member should have Matter 3, Life 3 and at least Prime 2 from the get-go, coming from their basic Paradigm by itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Essentially the issue is, that whenever Syndicate Magic comes up the usual answer is essentially a repetition of their basic Paradigm, instead of actual intricate manifestations of said Paradigm according to specific sphere levels. Yes, every Syndicate member understands the metaphysical power of Value. Every Syndicate member believes in the power of temporal assets like money. Every Syndicate member believes in investing worth to get excellent results.<br /> <br /> But what is the actual mental difference in understanding Value between a Syndicate member that has Matter 2, and one that has Matter 3?<br /> <br /> It's of a certain irony that the most exotic and hard-to-express paradigm and practice in Mage is based on economy and value, which is usually the opposite of creative magic. I personally love it. But it makes my brain hurt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, the buying Syndicate \u2018knows\u2019 that his secret hand signals, marked cash and encoded credit cards prompt the seller to turn aside the mundane items and present the top-grade ones. The seller, on the other hand, knows nothing except that somehow he felt he had to do that </div> </div> </div>That situation, once more, I'd simply consider a Mind procedure, and nothing that involves Matter and/or Prime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-11-2018, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:18:39-07:00","id":1205521,"title":"","content":"For a Syndicate op, their Sphere knowledge of Matter and Prime (or, rather, Primal Utility) represents not just their ability to &quot;throw money at a problem&quot;, but their understanding of how and where to throw that money. They know who to talk to, how to organize, where to get raw materials, and how to convince people to not only do the work, but to do it expeditiously. And if the Syndicate op doesn't personally know all these industry things, they can find the people who DO know. It's said that being able to gather talented people and turn them towards some specific undertaking is, itself, a talent. It's this talent - and the knowledge, experience, and guile needed to use it - that Syndicate ops cultivate.<br /> <br /> The cherry on top - that which pushes it all into the realms of Enlightened Science - is the Syndicate op's unflinching confidence in the efficacy of this action. Just as a mystic's Will propels arcane words and signs into the heights of True Magick. It just so happens that the Syndicate character's Will moves through those Human Resources and economic systems that make such broad Effects possible.<br /> <br /> Let's look at it on a smaller, more manageable scale. A Syndicate op needs to get across town quickly, and either can't or won't break out some borrowed hypertech. The character arranges a car and driver to show up, whether it's a private car and driver or a cab and cabbie. When he takes his place in the back seat, he gives the driver exact directions, and flashes a bit of cash, promising a generous tip if they get there quickly. If the car was a private one, and the driver kept on retainer, both are probably expensive. This means the Syndicate op is confident in their abilities, because the Syndicate only hires the best. If it's just a cab, like you'd find on any street corner, that generous bribe can bridge the performance gap, because the promise of profit is a great motivator. In either case, the Syndicate op's understanding of traffic, municipal planning, and distance allows him to plot a course that will maximize the ground they can cover (it might also help if the Syndicate op has GPS they can analyse with their Enlightened understanding). Even the Syndicate op's unflappable certainty in their ability to arrive &quot;early&quot; rubs off on the driver, increasing their performance via the power of positive thinking.<br /> <br /> All of this combines to a coincidental Correspondence 3 Effect, wherein the Syndicate op transports himself using his pre-prepared Instruments to his destination, faster than would be normally possible. It's not teleportation, but it is expedient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:29:43-07:00","id":1205522,"title":"","content":"Hmhmh.<br /> <br /> You know, Bluecho....<br /> I think I can suddenly summarize the core reason why it's so hard to express Syndicate Paradigm and Magick compared to all others, and why one tends to run into a strange metaphysical wall when applying the usual approach to Magick. Let's see if you agree.<br /> <br /> The Magick Sphere system and the way one builds effects is by default Process-Based, both in the practices as well as the Sphere-requirements.<br /> M20's 'Axis of Coincidence' writeup on page 533 sums it up well, and even as an example of using a taxi.<br /> But I think that, now that you describe things, the Syndicate Paradigm and Practice might be actually the one very thing in Mage that is actually, by RAW, different by being a Result-Based form of Sphere use and Paradigm. The classic 'Use Correspondence 3 to make a Taxi show up'.<br /> <br /> If you treat the Syndicate as the Result-Based exception in a Process-Based Sphere world, everything clicks into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-11-2018, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:57:01-07:00","id":1205524,"title":"","content":"Well, that is what it's like in the private sector. They expect results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T04:27:25-07:00","id":1205531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205522#post1205522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think that, now that you describe things, the Syndicate Paradigm and Practice might be actually the one very thing in Mage that is actually, by RAW, different by being a Result-Based form of Sphere use and Paradigm. The classic 'Use Correspondence 3 to make a Taxi show up'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well no, it's not, because I didn't set up a scenario where the <i>Magick</i> of the Effect is making a taxi show up. I explicitly stated that the Syndicate op was using <i>mundane</i> means to get the taxi into position (with, you know, a phone call or waving the vehicle down), and then employs that taxi as part of the <i>Instruments</i> used to cast the <i>actual Effect</i>, which was to get the character from Point A to Point B faster.<br /> <br /> No Magick was used to get the taxi there, it was just used to make that taxi do its job better. Which is entirely consistent with many other coincidental Effects from the books, like the many rotes used to get difficulty reductions on combat moves. Moreover, the use of Enlightened understanding to cover ground faster is a thing the Technocrats were doing since the Order of Reason days, starting with rotes developed by the Explorators back in Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:32:10-07:00","id":1205549,"title":"","content":"So what, a Syndicate Mage uses a brand new suit they're ordering as a Focus for their Matter effect, and then with Matter 2 they're reinforcing the suit to resist aesthetic and physical damage (acting like simple armour also).<br /> <br /> It's coincidental; this suit they got just happens to be a really great suit. The moment where they open the box and find something very nice is just a powerful moment, and they can invest magick in that moment I suppose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:55:22-07:00","id":1205553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205331-so-how-does-using-money-as-a-focus-for-matter-prime-work-in-practice?p=1205549#post1205549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what, a Syndicate Mage uses a brand new suit they're ordering as a Focus for their Matter effect, and then with Matter 2 they're reinforcing the suit to resist aesthetic and physical damage (acting like simple armour also).<br /> <br /> It's coincidental; this suit they got just happens to be a really great suit. The moment where they open the box and find something very nice is just a powerful moment, and they can invest magick in that moment I suppose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd interpret it more as the focus being the system of commerce that brought the suit into being in the first place. The institutions that can procure the materials, the R&amp;D department that can develop a better suit. and the factories that can produce the suit to the specifications required.<br /> <br /> That entire process is the Syndicate's focus. Their magic blurs the line between magic and mundane, because fundamentally their capitalist paradigm has, more successfully than NWO lead governance or Technocratic Science, become the defacto consensus of the west and all western influenced societies at a personal level.<br /> <br /> <br /> By this way, sending a suit to the cleaners to clean it up is Matter 2. Getting your people to install a swimming pool at the drop of a hat is Matter 4. Having the best gym, the best personal trainer, the best equipment, on hand to give you the workout of your life, that's Life 3. Having so much money you are able to have exactly what you need when you need it, that's Entropy 2.<br /> <br /> It's all about resources and influence. You want a building there by 6pm on a Friday? You got it. You want to be on a plane going to Fiji tomorrow? It's done. You want rewind live TV because you missed the start of your favourite series? Just give the right person a call and offer the correct amount.<br /> <br /> Money offers powers that the masses can only dream about. And that's the real magic, and the best part is that as long as the sleepers always look up and think &quot;some day that will be me&quot;, it will rarely be vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 04-11-2018, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:18:19-07:00","id":1205580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo....if you were in a game, what in detail would you describe your character doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Bluecho has nailed it. The supreme confidence of the mage in the action she performs and the complex systems behind it does the magick, but the action it's utterly mundane.<br /> <br /> A mage goes to a shop that sells stuff, tells the clerk what she wants, then offers the clerk a nice tip if she shows her the most expensive, best quality item. Enligthened people know the complex hypereconomical theory that assures us the item will be especial, but the hard fact it's that the stuff you've just bought automagically transforms into a superior item that adds whatever bonuses Matter can give.<br /> <br /> As a Syndicate friendly way to combine Matter/Prime in order to create matter, you would ask for something the store may have, but doesn't have at the moment (otherwise you would just buy it). You would insist when the employee tells you that item isn't in their existences, telling him to seek anyway (and bribe him with money), and presto, the object it's found in a box you promplty point or another inconspicuous place where stuff could be found. Of course, it was there all the time (exept it wasn't).<br /> <br /> Producing Wonders wouldn't be different albeit it that case you may want to follow the productive process of the item very closely, and then explain why each aspect of the item has it's property.<br /> <br /> Since Prime theory spouses that Quintessence it's Value, then coins and credit cards are natural stores of Quintessence. Coins aren't bateries, but Quintessence isn't &quot;energy&quot; either, but a conceptual construct under this Paradigm - the mage probably ain't going to eat a dollar bill to get power, but earning money in a Venture (or with a Node) may as well transfer the value/quintessence to her character sheet.<br /> While the Chorister of the group basks in the Quintessence of his church Node hearing the prayers, and then takes some blessed water to use as Tass, my mage would collect the donations. The amount of money may not seem worthy of an ex-syndicate tycoon, but the faithfull do generate &quot;value&quot; nevertheless - sometimes intention does matter. <hr />\u200b<br /> Of course, an Etherite may take a crazier take on all of this. Concepts like value, wealth and market may be entirely different for an Etherite. The potential of a <i>mad</i> <i>economic scientist</i> it's something I would like to see in practice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> The box approach isn't impossible, albeit I would like to know why the universe responds to boxes. Maybe it's a technobabble quantum-box that releases the sheer &quot;buying potential&quot; that money represents , and then, when opened after handling it in a specific geometrical pattern, locks the &quot;buying potential&quot; into a specific item that can be potentially bought with that coin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-11-2018, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}